{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when men strive.</b> One with another, and he intended to strike his fellow but struck the woman." "<b>And they push.</b> נְגִיפָה is nothing but a term of shoving and striking, as in ״פֶּן תִּגֹּף בָאֶבֶן רַגְלֶךָ״ (Psalms 91), ״בְּטֶרֶם יִתְנַגְּפוּ רַגְלֵיכֶם״ (Jeremiah 13), and ״לְאֶבֶן נֶגֶף״ (Isaiah 8)." "<b>And there be no harm.</b> To the woman." "<b>He shall be surely fined.</b> To pay the value of the offspring to the husband; they assess her — how much she was worth to be sold in the market to bring her value up on account of her pregnancy." "<b>Fined he shall be fined.</b> They exact money from him, as in ״וְעָנְשׁוּ אֹתוֹ מֵאָה כֶסֶף״ (Deuteronomy 22)." "<b>as the judge imposes upon him, etc.</b> When the husband brings suit against him in court to impose upon him a penalty for this." "<b>and he shall give.</b> The one who struck — the value of the offspring." "<b>with assessment.</b> According to the judges (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:41.516578341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}